[Music]  [Applause]  I'm here with Jeremy Godfrey the chair  of Burak Jeremy thanks for talking to us  tell us about this panel that you took  part in earlier today so the panel was  about what next for the European  institutions following the European  electronic communications code which  came into force last December and he's  been transposed over the next two years  so what I talked about was first of all  the role of Barrack in implementing that  code so Barracks role is to ensure a  consistent application of telecoms law  across europe and in the code there are  many sets of guidelines that Merrick is  mandated to do to make sure that the  national regulatory agencies the nras  across Europe applied the code in a  consistent manner so I first what I  talked about the work those elements of  the Verret work program and then I also  talked about the what I thought the  agenda might be for the incoming  Commission and incoming Parliament's who  are going to come in you're going to  take up their roles during later later  this year so the I'm quite sure that  digital issues will be a big theme for  the next commission I think it probably  they probably won't want to redo the  communications law again because it  because it will only be coming into full  force after two years and there would  need time to see how that works but I  think there will be a number of issues  related to the data economy  there are issues around new forms of  market power in the data economy for  example the platform's having large  amounts of data which it's difficult for  new entrants innovative new companies to  replicate there are issues around  privacy there are issues of societal  harm like fake news hate speech  disruption of elections and so forth  there are new forms of great new  potential benefits that can be got as  well in terms of things like  epidemiology you met here and medical  research keeping us the traffic moving  in smart cities and then of course that  all the potential applications of  artificial intelligence  they were just scraping the surface on  so I think there will be a huge number  of issues about how best to enable  Europe to take the you the benefits of  the digital economy but also how to  build confidence amongst end-users that  the data economy is is going to work for  them and isn't going to work against  their interests what are the  implications for the fibre community so  I think there's still a big push for  investments in fiber and in very high  capacity networks so there are a number  of regulatory issues around very high  capacity networks which Barrett will be  working on we are doing guidelines to  define what is meant by very high  capacity network so what technologies  that maybe complement fiber can so  qualify as very high capacity networks  what forms of regulatory  lighter forms of regulation might apply  stake to wholesale only networks of  which many members of the  fiber-to-the-home  Council Europe are in that are in that  business so I think from the fiber  community  there's nothing aims at once who give us  lots of inputs I think this morning I  had a meeting with some of the CEOs and  there was very interesting insights  about the problems they see some of the  some different types of competition  problems that they say that that they  think regulators and policy makers might  need to address so I think engagement  continued engagement with barek with  local regulators with the with the  Commission and with policy makers in  Member States going to be very important  you certainly seem to be very busy at  the moment to the benefit of our viewers  tell us what about barek and what it  does so Burak consists of the national  regulatory authorities for electronic  communications from each of the Member  States and then we also have other  people who attend beric meetings from  the ei countries and from accession  states and so forth and the primary role  of Barrack is to help facilitate a  consistent application of  telecommunications law across Europe so  in this year's work program most of what  we're doing is his guidelines for the  codes looking again the direct  guidelines on net neutrality so as I say  making sure that we have a very sensible  level of harmonization so that  pan-european operators investors and so  forth have a degree of predictability  about how individual national regulatory  authorities will apply them as a very  important angle for us but we as well as  as well as focusing on that we also have  a role in contributing to discussions  about forward-looking  issues so we're doing a piece of work on  the dynamics of investments in very high  capacity networks which is right at the  heart of what members of the  fiber-to-the-home Council Europe will  will care about so we want to understand  not what's the role of competition  what's the role of what can be done to  help help demand to develop fast what  should be done about about things like  copper switch off these are all issues  that will be part of that study so it's  a high-level study that looks at how all  those things interact with one another  and will then help us decide where we  need to focus our efforts we're also  looking at 5g so fibre of course will be  a very important component to 5g  networks I mean in a way 5g networks are  basically fiber networks with wireless  on the end of them and looking at again  what are all the issues regulators and  policy makers mean may need to look at  to enable innovation in the 5g ecosystem  enable innovation in IOT so we're  looking at some of those future looking  things and lastly Berek is wants to  wants to further deepen its engagement  with stakeholders so we are looking to  engage with the stakeholders of the  earlier stage in our projects so before  we actually put pen to paper and draft  guidelines  we'd like to kind of gather some input  we want to give ourselves a bit longer  to respond to our consultations and we  want to give them a  a formal opportunity to propose ideas  for our work program so those are the  three things that Barrett will be doing  this year working on the on the court on  the on a consistent application of  telecoms law in Europe contributing  forward-looking debates and engaging  more effectively the stakeholders well  thank you very much for speaking to us  it sounds like you've got a very busy  rest of the year ahead thank you thank  you very much  [Music]  you

